{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.shallow_of_no_deep_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.shallow_of_no_deep_cells","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L231-L251","doc":"**No deep cells ⇒ positive.**  If every cell sits above the threshold, `P(λ) = 0` and the\nweight is positive.\n\nAt `q₀` a below-threshold cell needs content `≤ −3`, hence `≥ 4` rows.  **Under convention C**\nthat made this exactly the statement that every `ℓ(λ) ≤ 3` block carries a positive weight,\n`(8,1)` included.  **Under D read `ℓ(λ) ≤ 2`**: the `ℓ(λ) = 3` blocks are not positive but\nidentically zero, and in any case they fail this theorem's own `hnd` hypothesis, since under D\na cell of content `−2` sits *exactly* on the threshold.  The theorem itself is unchanged and\ngeneric — only which diagrams can satisfy its hypotheses moves with the convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_sign","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L178-L229","doc":"**`sign(s_λ) = (−1)^{P(λ)}`, `P(λ)` the number of BELOW-threshold cells.**\n\nThe Wenzl principal specialisation `Q^{n(λ)}·∏(1 − Q^r·Q^{c})/∏(1 − Q^{h})` has sign exactly\n`(−1)` to the number of cells whose content lies *below* the threshold `c* = −log_Q(Q^r)`.\n\nBoth the `Q^{n(λ)}` prefactor and the denominator's shape drop out: the former is positive,\nthe latter contributes `(−1)^{|λ|}` which merges with the numerator's `(−1)^{#above}` to leave\n`(−1)^{#below}`.  So a *global* property of the diagram (its size) is invisible, and only the\n*deep* cells matter.\n\nHypotheses are the honest minimum: `Q > 1` (the substrate regime `q > 1`), hooks positive\n(automatic for a Young diagram), and no cell exactly on the threshold (`hnd`) — without which\nthe parity is genuinely undefined, not merely hard to prove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.card_above_add_card_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.card_above_add_card_below","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L159-L174","doc":"**Above-threshold and below-threshold cells partition the diagram.**  Given no cell sits\nexactly *on* the threshold, the two counts sum to the number of cells — the bookkeeping that\nlets the denominator's `(−1)^{|λ|}` be absorbed into the numerator's parity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_num_factor_neg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_num_factor_neg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L152-L156","doc":"**The threshold criterion.**  A numerator factor is negative exactly when the cell sits\n*above* the threshold, i.e. when `Q^r·Q^{c(x)} > 1`.  This is the only place the content\nenters, and it enters through a single scalar comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_den_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_den_sign","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L138-L148","doc":"**The denominator contributes the fixed sign `(−1)^{|λ|}`** — it depends on the cell\n*count* alone, not on the shape of the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_den_factor_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_den_factor_neg","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L130-L136","doc":"**Every denominator factor is negative.**  A hook length is at least `1`, and `Q > 1`, so\n`Q^{h} > 1` and `1 − Q^{h} < 0`.  No cell escapes this — which is what makes the denominator's\nsign depend only on the *number* of cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.neg_one_pow_card_neg_mul_prod_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold.neg_one_pow_card_neg_mul_prod_pos","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaSignThreshold.lean#L98-L126","doc":"**Sign of a finite product.**  Multiplying a product of nonzero reals by `(−1)` raised to\nthe number of negative factors makes it positive.  This is the combinatorial engine behind the\nwhole file: it turns \"count the negative factors\" into an actual sign statement. ","signatureChunk":0}]}